      "message": "I don\u0027t think this does what you want\n\nFuture.get(timeout) \u003d\u003e This just waits for the Future to complete. The timeout is for the calling thread. _Calling thread_ waits at most |timeout| time for the future to complete. If timeout is exceeded, it just means the calling thread won\u0027t continue waiting, however the _awaited thread_ (the blocked thread / the thread that actually executes readClipboardFromVm()) would still continue to run.\n\nSame goes for `InterruptedException`. This means the calling thread is interrupted before the Futre.get() deadline is reached. It does _not_ mean the awaited thread is interrupted.\n\nSo what you want is to call Future.get() with timeout,\nIf `InterruptedException` or `TimeoutException` is caught, call Future.cancel() on the pending Future, so that the awaited thread is cancelled / interrupted. (Otherwise it would keep lingering in the background)\n\nThat being said the Future.cancel() still probably won\u0027t do what you want, because readClipboardFromVm() does not check the Thread.isInterrupted() state.",
